        {
          "id": "20260822-daily-prophet-001-p02",
          "text": "2. Early wrongs of the Moslem; justification in taking up arms, if taken ii",
          "language": "en",
          "sourceRefs": [
            "20260822-daily-prophet-001-source"
          ],
          "substantive": true,
          "aiOriginal": false,
          "quotation": false,
          "quotationVerified": true,
          "editorialOperations": [
            "whitespace-normalization",
            "boilerplate-exclusion",
            "source-paragraph-preservation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "20260822-daily-prophet-001-p03",
          "text": "3. Commencement of the war; the Koreish being public enemy were liable to be treated as such _ib._",
          "language": "en",
          "sourceRefs": [
            "20260822-daily-prophet-001-source"
          ],
          "substantive": true,
          "aiOriginal": false,
          "quotation": false,
          "quotationVerified": true,
          "editorialOperations": [
            "whitespace-normalization",
            "boilerplate-exclusion",
            "source-paragraph-preservation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "20260822-daily-prophet-001-p04",
          "text": "4. But the Moslems could not take up arms to redress their wrongs under certain circumstances iii",
          "language": "en",
          "sourceRefs": [
            "20260822-daily-prophet-001-source"
          ],
          "substantive": true,
          "aiOriginal": false,
          "quotation": false,
          "quotationVerified": true,
          "editorialOperations": [
            "whitespace-normalization",
            "boilerplate-exclusion",
            "source-paragraph-preservation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "20260822-daily-prophet-001-p05",
          "text": "5. Moslems otherwise engaged at Medina had no intention of suffering the horrors of war by taking the initiative, but were in imminent danger from the enemy iv",
          "language": "en",
          "sourceRefs": [
            "20260822-daily-prophet-001-source"
          ],
          "substantive": true,
          "aiOriginal": false,
          "quotation": false,
          "quotationVerified": true,
          "editorialOperations": [
            "whitespace-normalization",
            "boilerplate-exclusion",
            "source-paragraph-preservation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "20260822-daily-prophet-001-p06",
          "text": "6. The Koreish first attacked the Moslems at Medina. They could not forbear the escape of the Moslems v",
          "language": "en",
          "sourceRefs": [
            "20260822-daily-prophet-001-source"
          ],
          "substantive": true,
          "aiOriginal": false,
          "quotation": false,
          "quotationVerified": true,
          "editorialOperations": [
            "whitespace-normalization",
            "boilerplate-exclusion",
            "source-paragraph-preservation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "20260822-daily-prophet-001-p07",
          "text": "7. Three battles waged by the Koreish against Mohammad--Badr, Ohad, and Ahzab: these wars on the Moslem side were purely in defence, not waged even to redress their wrongs or re-establish their rights vii",
          "language": "en",
          "sourceRefs": [
            "20260822-daily-prophet-001-source"
          ],
          "substantive": true,
          "aiOriginal": false,
          "quotation": false,
          "quotationVerified": true,
          "editorialOperations": [
            "whitespace-normalization",
            "boilerplate-exclusion",
            "source-paragraph-preservation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "20260822-daily-prophet-001-p08",
          "text": "8. The battle of Badr was defensive on the part of Mohammad. Reasons for the same viii",
          "language": "en",
          "sourceRefs": [
            "20260822-daily-prophet-001-source"
          ],
          "substantive": true,
          "aiOriginal": false,
          "quotation": false,
          "quotationVerified": true,
          "editorialOperations": [
            "whitespace-normalization",
            "boilerplate-exclusion",
            "source-paragraph-preservation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "20260822-daily-prophet-001-p09",
          "text": "9. Mohammad at Medina, owing to the attacks, inroads, and threatening gatherings of the Koreish and other tribes, had hardly time to think of offensive measures xi",
          "language": "en",
          "sourceRefs": [
            "20260822-daily-prophet-001-source"
          ],
          "substantive": true,
          "aiOriginal": false,
          "quotation": false,
          "quotationVerified": true,
          "editorialOperations": [
            "whitespace-normalization",
            "boilerplate-exclusion",
            "source-paragraph-preservation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "20260822-daily-prophet-001-p10",
          "text": "10. Armed opposition of the Koreish to the Moslem pilgrims from Medina in the vicinity of Mecca. The truce of Hodeibia xv",
